narrative:
## Your L0 Showcase

This lesson has nothing new to learn. Instead, you'll use EVERY concept from L0 in one program:

- Variables (`let` and `var`)
- Types (Int, Bool, Str)
- Math operations (`+`, `-`, `*`, `/`, `+=`, parentheses)
- Comparisons (`==`, `!=`, `<`, `>`, `<=`, `>=`)
- Strings (concat, length, uppercase, lowercase)
- Conditions (`if`, `elif`, `else`, `&&`, `||`, `!`)
- Loops (`while` and `for`)

### The Showcase Program

```xiom
fn main() {
  let name: Str = "Morgan";
  var score: Int = 0;
  let target: Int = 100;

  let greeting: Str = string.str_concat("Welcome, ", string.str_upper(name));
  io.println(greeting);

  let name_len: Int = string.str_len(name);
  let bonus: Int = name_len * 2;
  score += bonus;

  io.print("Starting score: ");
  io.println(score);

  var round: Int = 1;
  while round <= 3 {
    io.print("Round ");
    io.print(round);
    io.print(": +10 points! ");
    score += 10;
    io.print("Score: ");
    io.println(score);
    round += 1;
  }

  if score >= target && score % 2 == 0 {
    io.println("Amazing! You hit the target with an even score!");
  } elif score >= target {
    io.println("Great job! You hit the target!");
  } else {
    io.println("Keep practicing — you're getting closer!");
  }

  let is_winner: Bool = score >= target;
  io.print("Winner status: ");
  io.println(is_winner);
}
```

This program uses strings, math, `var`, `let`, `while`, `if/elif/else`, comparisons, and logical operators — all working together!

### You Built This!

Every concept in this program is something you learned in L0. Variables hold your data. Math transforms it. Strings display it. Conditions make decisions. Loops repeat. You now speak the language of programming!

